---
/**
 * ProblemSection — frames why AI-readiness matters before the how.
 */
---

<section
	id="problem"
	aria-labelledby="problem-heading"
	class="bg-surface-raised py-section-y"
>
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-4 sm:px-6">
		<div class="flex max-w-prose flex-col gap-4">
			<h2
				id="problem-heading"
				class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight"
			>
				AI code is only as good as your Figma
			</h2>
			<p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
				AI tools turn Figma into code. When layers are unnamed, structure is
				loose, and tokens are missing, the generated output drifts from your
				intent.
			</p>
			<p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
				The time you saved on handoff goes back into cleanup. DesignReady
				catches these gaps in the design, before a single line is generated.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
